cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "sensei-slides: an agent skill for lecture and seminar slides that audiences can follow"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Naito
    given-names: Kanato
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/naito-kanato/sensei-slides"
abstract: >-
  An agent skill that makes lecture and seminar slides, speaker notes and a
  commentable notes page, either as an AI-taught course built one session at a
  time or as a single talk from a paper or textbook. It audits the inferential
  distance for a stated audience (the premises the listener must supply), plans
  the story as questions and answers, has separate agents write and review, and
  checks the rendered slides with scripts.
keywords:
  - presentation slides
  - instructional design
  - LLM agents
  - inferential distance
  - curse of knowledge
